WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.960
Safe!

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.250
You really can't lower your guard in the Majors.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.610
<i>Shigeno is at his limit.</i>

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.970
<i>Why isn't the boss subbing him out?</i>

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.650
<i>Get a good taste of this, Shigeno.</i>

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.930
<i>The wall of the Majors starts here.</i>

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.410
<i>Up till now, I've only concentrated on polishing my fastball, but...</i>

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:55.010
<i>with just that, I can't break through the wall of the Majors.</i>

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:59.340
<i>I don't know how far I can go, having been originally right-handed, but...</i>

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.760
<i>I have to find a breaking ball that fits me!</i>

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:05.300
Play!

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.850
<i>Sorry, but...</i>

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:11.810
<i>I'm not planning on staying at this shabby stage for many months!</i>

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:16.690
<i>Time to hurry up, produce some results, and rise up to the Majors!</i>

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.450
Strike!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.140
<i>He's throwing quite the fastball.</i>

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.380
<i>But,</i>

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.520
<i>it's not a pitch I can't hit!</i>

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.320
<i>Curve!?</i>

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.530
Strike out!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:40.660
<i>I've just had problems finding a breaking ball that fits me till now.</i>

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.040
Strike!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.890
<i>If I learn how to use breaking balls,</i>

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:49.010
<i>I can also...</i>

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.720
<i>pitch this way!</i>

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.350
Strike out!

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.480
Out!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.060
Okay!

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.410
All right!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.340
Out!

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.050
Strike out!

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.900
All right!

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.680
Nice pitching!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.130
You're doing great, rookie!

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:53.840
Bravo! Bravo! Bravo!

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:54.360
Bravo! Bravo! Bravo!

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.610
Bravo! Bravo! Bravo!

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.780
You're so great, Shigeno!

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.800
You've finished the five innings you were responsible for, but...

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.480
do you want to continue?

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.210
He's asking if you want to continue.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.660
Oh, okay, okay! It's not a problem at all.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:12.380
Rather, it's basically the pitcher's responsibility to pitch the game from beginning to end.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.470
What a promising rookie!

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.260
<i>This guy is unexpectedly skillful.</i>

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.520
<i>To think he could learn to throw breaking balls this well in just a couple of days...</i>

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.400
<i>But...</i>

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.230
Damn!

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.970
How could we only get one hit in five innings against a rookie!?

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.280
There's no reason to worry, boss.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.550
Gibson!

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.880
That guy is an imitation of a pitcher.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:45.710
We'll most likely catch him soon.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.630
If it suits you,

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.980
I'm prepared to enter the batter's box anytime.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:58.610
Well then, in the exhibition game between the Falcons and the Cougars...

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:02.220
Right now they're finishing the bottom half of the sixth inning, with the Cougars leading with 3-0!

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.770
The Cougars' starting pitcher, the rookie Shigeno,

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:10.980
has shown pitching prowess that has held the Falcons' batters to one hit.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:11.610
However,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.650
this time the Falcons lead off with the heart of their order, starting from the two spot.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.910
What kind of pitching will the rookie, Shigeno, show?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:25.870
Play!

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:29.600
<i>The first time through you cornered them with fastballs and finished them with breaking balls.</i>

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.550
<i>I think you should make fastballs the main constituent the second time through and lure them with breaking balls.</i>

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.470
<i>Then what about the third time through...</i>

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.990
<i>After all, they're the lower Triple A...</i>

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.140
<i>If I just mix in some breaking balls,</i>

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.850
<i>they won't be able to...</i>

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:49.390
<i>do anything!</i>

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.220
All right!

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.220
Yes!

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.740
He hit it really well.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.720
Coach, he's thrown 100 pitches with the last one.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.130
It's only the second hit, but he is a rookie after all.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:16.010
It would be best if he left feeling good about his first time taking the mound.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.300
Feeling good!?

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:26.600
Leaving the mound with such a muddied impression isn't the best thing for him.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.320
Okay, Gibson! Go for it after this one!

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.400
Yes, sir.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:50.160
<i>It took time to adjust to his variety of pitches and timing the first time seeing him.</i>

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:56.000
<i>Also, the second time through the order, we needed to identify what kind of pitches would come.</i>

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.520
Ball!

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:05.640
Ball two!

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:14.980
<i>If you don't have the control to properly guide breaking balls to their location, they won't have any cut.</i>

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.520
<i>It seems that only his fastball is fast, but...</i>

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.110
<i>in the Minors,</i>

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.030
<i>a pitcher of your level,</i>

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:23.820
<i>there're 50,000 just like you!</i>

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.620
Safe!

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:38.540
C-Coach!

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:40.730
What are you doing, rookie?

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.220
Put your spirit into it!

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:47.860
<i>Damn!</i>

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.330
<i>What's happening?</i>

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:51.940
<i>My pitching that worked so well till now...</i>

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.230
<i>In this inning, it isn't working at all!</i>

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.530
Attention please! Batting, number one,

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.830
Joe Gibson Junior!

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:13.610
<i>J... </i>

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:17.070
<i>Junior?</i>

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.750
Joe Gibson... 

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.850
Junior, he said?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.440
Shigeno!

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.790
This won't work any longer.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:30.520
They've completely seen through your breaking balls.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.870
It was too early to use them in a real game, after all.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:33.880
Fox...

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.510
Joe Gibson Jr...

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.030
Who is he?

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:41.320
What do you mean, "who"? It's Gibson Jr!

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:45.240
That great ace, with 300 victories...

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.370
He's Joe Gibson's son.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:56.050
<i>Gibson's... </i>

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.710
<i>son?</i>

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:01.070
In last year's All-American Draft,

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.950
he was picked by the Falcons' Texas Raiders:

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.340
A highly touted rookie.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.450
It's what you'd expect from Gibson's son.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:09.890
While he's only 19 years old,

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:13.760
it's widely believed that he's going to rise to the Majors as soon as this year.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:17.730
During the season, he's an annoying pinch hitter who plays third base.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.030
Anyway, lure him with your breaking balls.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.690
Then use your fastball, which you've got confidence in, for the real duel.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.060
<i>G-Gibson had...</i>

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.110
<i>a son like that?</i>

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.120
<i>I never imagined...</i>

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.120
<i>that in a place like this,</i>

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.550
<i>before I faced Gibson,</i>

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.920
<i>I could have a showdown with his son!</i>

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:51.280
This is a free fansub.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:51.280
Not for sale or rent.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:02.400
<i>I came here aiming for where Joe Gibson is, the Major League.</i>

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:07.880
<i>I don't have any grudges or hard feelings for him killing my father any longer.</i>

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:10.260
<i>I only want to...</i>

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:13.770
<i>show my grown-up figure to that man.</i>

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.950
<i>No, I have to show him.</i>

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:21.870
<i>So I can prove that Honda Shigeharu's heir is here!</i>

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.090
Play!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.750
<i>No outs and the bases loaded...</i>

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:30.930
<i>Lacking control and cut, your breaking ball won't work.</i>

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:32.380
<i>Use your fastball!</i>

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:37.350
<i>Use your supreme fastball and overcome this barrier!</i>

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:42.230
<i>Joe Gibson Jr, huh?</i>

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:43.940
<i>For now,</i>

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:47.270
<i>if this could be called my preliminary before facing Gibson,</i>

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:51.450
<i>I can't lose to his kid here!</i>

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:13.810
<i>He hit it in the sweet part of the bat and lifted it up...</i>

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:16.810
Well, it'll be a good experience.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.620
Umpire!

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.440
We're changing pitchers!

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:43.450
Nice batting! It's what you'd expect from the first pick in the All-American Draft.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:47.130
Someone like me, who got in through the tryouts, can't beat someone like you.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:50.820
But,

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.050
it definitely won't end like this!

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:56.720
Tell your dad too!

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:02.060
That Honda Jr is definitely coming to the Majors to defeat you, father and son!

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.100
What? Damn it!

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.610
Why am I crying?

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.480
<i>Honda?</i>

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:15.730
<i>That is...</i>

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.450
<i>Honda Jr!?</i>

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:28.090
Is that true?

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.040
This is surprising!

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.740
He speaks Japanese?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:32.920
So that's how it was.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.300
So you...

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.380
were that dead idiot's son?

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:40.300
What was that?

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:42.000
What did you say just now!?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.830
Try and say it again!

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.530
I'll say it as many times as you'd like.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:50.020
Who would've thought that the son of the idiotic player who died from having a bean ball hit his head,

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:53.440
would come to America to play baseball?

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:58.860
It's no wonder I can't feel an ounce of talent in you, you third-rate pitcher.

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:05.540
Hurry up, return to Japan, and die playing pretend baseball, just like your father.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.380
I'll kill you!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:13.120
I won't forgive anyone who makes fun of my father!

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:17.220
What is he doing?

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:18.680
This is bad!

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.390
Hey, hey, what's with that attitude?

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:26.000
Because your stupid dad died,

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.770
I was stuck living on that island country for two years afterwards.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:34.740
Rather than this, shouldn't you apologize for your papa?

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.530
Bastard!

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.990
Let me go, damn it!

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:47.090
Wait! Damn you!

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:51.260
Let go of me!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.660
Fox?

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:13.360
You really put on a show back there.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:19.310
I don't know what kind of connection you have with Gibson Jr, but...

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.490
that disorderly conduct was bad.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:24.860
Instead of the grand slam home run you gave up to the other team,

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.750
that'll be the bigger problem.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:33.880
Well, first of all, you won't be able to avoid being fined or put under house arrest.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.680
If you're unlucky, you'll drop down to Double A.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.910
Also be prepared for a release as the worst case scenario.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.320
Release?

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:43.050
What's a release?

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.140
It means you'll be fired.

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.140
Fired!?

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:58.980
<i>Tell your dad too!</i>

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:06.160
<i>That Honda Jr is definitely coming to the Majors to defeat you, father and son!</i>

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.700
<i>Honda Jr, huh?</i>

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:18.680
Wha-!?

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.260
100 dollar fine?

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:22.180
Only?

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.440
Yeah.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:28.550
Well, it's your first offense after all, and we can see that you show remorse for what you did, so we decided on a kind punishment.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.140
During the season we couldn't do this.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:33.180
He's saying you're getting a kind punishment.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.230
Isn't that great, Shigeno?

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.560
Yahoo!

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:37.780
Thank you! Thank you! 

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:38.700
Thank you! Thank you! 

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:41.880
Thank you very much, boss!

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:46.620
But, in the end, this was just the punishment for the disorderly conduct.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:50.580
The essential skill, your pitching, was lacking.

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:56.060
In your first game you managed to deceive your opponents till the sixth inning, but next time they'll figure it out quicker.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:59.870
N-No, don't be so pessimistic!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.260
It's only that I still lack training with breaking balls.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.430
If I just continue to work on them- 

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.430
Shigeno.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.760
It's unfortunate, but you're released.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:11.570
What are you saying?

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:12.930
You're discharging Shigeno?

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.200
Is there a problem with that?

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:20.700
B-But, didn't the owner approve of the plan to develop the Japanese player, Shigeno, as a long term goal?

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:21.540
Miller-kun.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:27.110
You know about the Los Angeles Pegasus' Japanese pitcher, Onodera, right?

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:28.870
What? Yes, of course.

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:32.620
He's joining our team.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.000
Onodera is?

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.360
Exactly.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.720
In other words, he's not an immediately "usable weapon,"

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:41.060
and doesn't attract Japanese fans.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.970
Not to mention that he caused a public disturbance. We no longer have any need for Shigeno.

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:56.830
W-Wait a moment!

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:59.350
This is inconvenient, really inconvenient for me!

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:03.530
Double A- No, Single A is okay! Please don't fire me!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.870
It's an order from the owner.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:08.490
It's a pity, but it's already been decided.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:16.790
Though, there are still some other teams that are holding special Minor League tryouts.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:22.960
It's in Tennessee though, but I've prepared a letter of introduction.

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:25.800
Take this with you and visit them.

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:27.880
I hope to see you shine on a new field. 

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:47.210
<i>What a mess.</i>

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:49.820
<i>What have I been doing?</i>

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:54.200
<i>I came to America in high spirits...</i>

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:56.300
<i>and had never been to tryouts before.</i>

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:58.950
<i>At the Major League camp,</i>

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:03.750
<i>Sanchez showed me the difference in power between us, and I lost my confidence.</i>

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:09.760
<i>And, sure enough, in the exhibition game, I was showered with blows and was demoted to the Minors.</i>

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:13.930
<i>Trying to do something about it,
the breaking balls I learned didn't work.</i>

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.980
<i>And this is the result.</i>

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:27.680
<i>Who would've thought that the son of the idiotic player who died from having a bean ball hit his head,</i>

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:31.360
<i>would come to America to play baseball?</i>

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:36.960
<i>It's no wonder I can't feel an ounce of talent in you, you third-rate pitcher.</i>

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:43.850
<i>Hurry up, return to Japan, and die playing pretend baseball, just like your father.</i>

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.950
Not only did I totally lack power,

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.230
but he even insulted my father as well!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.500
Forgive me... father.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.680
Forgive me... father.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:08.190
<i>Maybe joining the Majors after just finishing high school was too much after all.</i>

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:17.870
What do you think you're doing, Shigeno!?

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.240
Leaving without saying anything!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.790
I told you that I'd accompany you to the airport!

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.120
Fox!?

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.960
Get in. You're acting distant!

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:30.460
Even if it was only for a short time, we're comrades who formed a battery!

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:36.620
Sorry, Fox.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.050
S-Sanchez!?

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:44.940
Yo.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:49.450
Well, I heard that the idiot got fired.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:54.060
Since he was off today, he thought that he could come ridicule you while he was doing an errand anyway, it seems.

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:55.920
W-What's that?

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.370
W-What's that?

00:20:57.780 --> 00:20:59.280
I'm just joking.

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:00.040
Just joking.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:05.340
I heard you got hit by Gibson Jr and flared up.

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:11.880
The sad thing is, it's your disposition that led you to this.

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:15.390
After our quarrel,

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:18.660
it seems you worked on breaking balls.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.350
He says that you've been working on breaking balls.

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:23.750
What? You got a problem with that?

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:25.270
Don't underestimate the Majors!

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:30.020
With such an idea, you will never become a Major Leaguer.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:36.400
Do you think I could pitch this well when I was your age?

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:42.890
It took me over ten years to attain the skill level I have today.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.120
No,

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:49.420
as I got weaker, I had no other way than to learn this skill.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:54.070
Unlike in my youth, when I could challenge my opponents with just fastballs.

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.480
You're still young.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:02.560
Rather than imitating an old man,
concentrate on your fastball more!

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:07.750
If you can gain true control over your serious fastballs,

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:10.440
you'll be able to strike out even Bolton and Gibson Jr!

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:21.020
Take your time and work on your game!

00:22:22.280 --> 00:22:25.060
I know you can dig up the results.

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:28.100
Make your way up slowly... but surely!

00:22:29.770 --> 00:22:33.230
I'll be waiting for you... in the Majors!

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:39.480
I have no time to be depressed! 

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:13.350
I've been fired! 

00:24:14.110 --> 00:24:16.610
What am I going to do from now on?

00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:20.230
Oh well, I can't keep worrying about it forever.

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:22.230
I'll make a fresh start in a new place!

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:23.980
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:25.200
Perfect Score in Courage!

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:27.800
Run to the stage of your dreams!
